# Runs when all-tunnel-certbot.service fails (OnFailure=). It makes the failure impossible to miss on the node itself:
#   a CRITICAL line in the journal (`journalctl -p crit -t all-tunnel-certbot`), a marker file that `the deploy tool status` reports, and a wall
#   message to whoever is logged in. The service itself stays in the failed state (`systemctl --failed`) until the next run succeeds, which clears the
#   marker (all-tunnel-cert-check does).
# The mail to the owner does not come from here (a node has no mail and no secret to send one with): it comes from the site monitor (14 and 5 days left,
# the site's monitor) and from the independent CT watcher, which both read the certificate the node SERVES.
[Unit]
Description=The ALL tunnel node's certificate renewal FAILED

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/logger -p daemon.crit -t all-tunnel-certbot "node certificate renewal FAILED: read journalctl -u all-tunnel-certbot, fix it, then systemctl start all-tunnel-certbot"
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'date -u +%%FT%%TZ > /var/lib/all-tunnel/certbot.failed'
ExecStart=-/usr/bin/wall "all-tunnel: the node certificate renewal FAILED (journalctl -u all-tunnel-certbot)"
